# SRG-APP-000705-WSR-000110  -  CAT II
# The web server must disable accounts when the accounts are no longer
# associated to a user.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations, then kept
# by hand. Edit this file to change how this requirement is assessed here;
# it is read at run time. Regenerating refreshes the benchmark text in place
# and leaves the criteria, the determination and any verification block as
# they are.

id:              SRG-APP-000705-WSR-000110
group:           V-264338
severity:        medium
cat:             CAT II
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       manual
confidence:      derived
revised:         yes
cci:             CCI-003628
control_rev5:    AC-2

contribution:    Splunk cannot itself determine that an account no longer belongs to a
                 user, so its contribution is to honor the disable or delete issued by
                 whatever authority holds the account lifecycle at the next authentication.

external:        The enterprise directory service or identity provider determines when an
                 account is no longer associated to a user and must push the disable or
                 delete.
external:        Where accounts are provisioned through SCIM, the provisioning authority
                 issues the deprovisioning call; the product carries the receiving path
                 only.
external:        The organization's offboarding and periodic account review procedures are
                 outside the application.
external:        An assessor confirms the lifecycle authority and its disassociation
                 handling, because the application exposes no value to read.

manual_reason:   The product exposes no value that determines whether an account is still
                 associated to a user or disables it on that basis; the account lifecycle
                 authority is confirmed by the assessor.

citation:        The three conditions repeat the defects corrected in
                 SRG-APP-000700-WSR-000100 and SRG-APP-000705-AU-000110. authType
                 not_equals Splunk forces delegated authentication the check text does not
                 ask for and fails an instance whose account lifecycle is managed
                 procedurally, which is over-reach against the documented default of Splunk
                 (authentication.conf.spec:30-33). server.conf [teleport_supervisor]
                 disabled already defaults to false, launched, and governs SCIM
                 authorization token handling rather than account state
                 (server.conf.spec:6584-6591). web-features.conf
                 [feature:identity_sidecar_scim] enabled defaults to true and only decides
                 whether Splunk Web shows Automated User Management controls in the SAML
                 configuration dialog (web-features.conf.spec:400-410); a dialog toggle
                 cannot disable an account. This SRG carries no product STIG rule, so
                 neither value has any source text behind it. The inventory for this
                 requirement is also unusable: the keys it lists under server.conf
                 [teleport_supervisor] - Splunk, Web, scimSupportedDomains and
                 scsSyncUserDeletes - are not settings of that stanza, which defines only
                 disabled, and none of the last two appear in any .conf.spec in the 10.4.2
                 set, so no criterion can be written over them.
finding:         No application-layer finding is available: Splunk has no setting that
                 detects an account with no associated user or disables it, so the assessor
                 records the identity authority that performs the disable; raise a finding
                 only where no authority outside the application does so.
